🚀 Git Push — Complete Commands (PowerShell Me)
Bhai ye exact commands hain. PowerShell me ek-ek line chalao. Copy-paste ready hai.

⚡ Quick One-Shot (Agar Sab Ready Hai)
PowerShell me ye ek line paste karo:

powershell
cd C:\Users\HP\multi-agent-gpu-cluster-manager; git add .; git commit -m "Update project files"; git push
Enter dabao. Done! ✅

📋 Detailed Step-by-Step (Recommended)
PowerShell me ek-ek karke chalao:

1️⃣ Project folder me jao:
powershell
cd C:\Users\HP\multi-agent-gpu-cluster-manager
2️⃣ Kya changed hai dekho:
powershell
git status
Output dekh:

Red files = uncommitted changes

Green files = staged (already added)

3️⃣ Sab files add karo:
powershell
git add .
4️⃣ Verify staged files:
powershell
git status
Green me dikhni chahiye saari files.

5️⃣ Commit karo (message ke saath):
powershell
git commit -m "Update: Add README and project structure"
⚠️ "Update: Add README and project structure" ki jagah apna message likh sakta hai.

Example messages:

powershell
git commit -m "Add backend agents implementation"
git commit -m "Fix scheduler agent logic"
git commit -m "Update README documentation"
git commit -m "Add GPU simulator module"
6️⃣ Push karo:
powershell
git push
Output:

text
